From 30394030106a6b78388ade892d1616bbce02f8a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Sheremeta <gshereme@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2015 16:54:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] engine: fixed NPE findbugs introduced in 1bfc9d0

Change-Id: Ib125a84415d84b2d4cda661b04719b5f5fa470d8
Signed-off-by: Greg Sheremeta <gshereme@redhat.com>

diff --git a/backend/manager/modules/bll/src/main/java/org/ovirt/engine/core/bll/RemoveVmCommand.java b/backend/manager/modules/bll/src/main/java/org/ovirt/engine/core/bll/RemoveVmCommand.java
index 0de4946a62b..a028e4ab465 100644
--- a/backend/manager/modules/bll/src/main/java/org/ovirt/engine/core/bll/RemoveVmCommand.java
+++ b/backend/manager/modules/bll/src/main/java/org/ovirt/engine/core/bll/RemoveVmCommand.java
@@ -349,7 +349,7 @@ public class RemoveVmCommand<T extends RemoveVmParameters> extends VmCommand<T>
             try {
                 failedRemoveCinderDisks = future.get().getActionReturnValue();
             } catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
-                failedRemoveCinderDisks.addAll(cinderDisks);
+                failedRemoveCinderDisks = cinderDisks;
                 log.error("Exception", e);
             }
         }
-- 
2.25.1

        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by an attempt to add elements from the `cinderDisks` list to `failedRemoveCinderDisks` in the catch block, which could lead to a Null Pointer Exception (NPE) if `failedRemoveCinderDisks` was not initialized properly. This situation arose when an exception occurred during the execution of a future task, and the code did not handle the initialization of `failedRemoveCinderDisks` correctly before attempting to add to it.

        Commit message:
        engine: fixed NPE findbugs introduced in 1bfc9d0

Change-Id: Ib125a84415d84b2d4cda661b04719b5f5fa470d8
Signed-off-by: Greg Sheremeta <gshereme@redhat.com>  

        Patch:
              */
     private Collection<CinderDisk> removeCinderDisks() {
         Collection<CinderDisk> failedRemoveCinderDisks = null;
         if (getParameters().isRemoveDisks()) {
             List<CinderDisk> cinderDisks =
                     ImagesHandler.filterDisksBasedOnCinder(getVm().getDiskMap().values());
             RemoveAllVmCinderDisksParameters param = new RemoveAllVmCinderDisksParameters(getVmId(), cinderDisks);
             param.setParentHasTasks(!getReturnValue().getVdsmTaskIdList().isEmpty());
             Future<VdcReturnValueBase> future = CommandCoordinatorUtil.executeAsyncCommand(
                     VdcActionType.RemoveAllVmCinderDisks,
                     withRootCommandInfo(param, getActionType()),
                     cloneContextAndDetachFromParent());
             try {
                 failedRemoveCinderDisks = future.get().getActionReturnValue();
             } catch (InterruptedException | ExecutionException e) {
-                failedRemoveCinderDisks.addAll(cinderDisks);
+                failedRemoveCinderDisks = cinderDisks;
                 log.error("Exception", e);
             }
         }
         return failedRemoveCinderDisks;
     }



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Code statements:
        <text1>
        <text2>
        ...
        <textN>

Code statements:
```java
Collection<CinderDisk> failedRemoveCinderDisks = null;
failedRemoveCinderDisks.addAll(cinderDisks);
failedRemoveCinderDisks = cinderDisks;
```

